@hafalconwood • 28 September 2026
Please join us for our Sixth Form Open Evening on Tuesday 13th October 5pm-7pm at Harris Academy Falconwood.
@hafalconwood • 25 September 2026
Join us at Harris Academy Falconwood Sixth Form Open Evening on Tuesday 13th October 5pm-7pm! Discover our A Level and Level 3 CTEC courses, meet staff and students, and tour the academy. We look forward to welcoming current Year 11 students and their families. No tickets needed.
@hafalconwood • 23 September 2026
LEGO Masters Young Engineers Enrichment Gets Off to a Flying Start! Students were challenged to design and build their own LEGO creations, including moving models powered by motors, using problem-solving skills to bring their designs to life.
@hafalconwood • 21 September 2026
@hafalconwood • 17 July 2026
Our students had an amazing time enjoying lots of sporting activities on the final day of term. From teamwork challenges to friendly competitions, the day was filled with energy, enthusiasm, and plenty of smiles!
@hafalconwood • 15 July 2026
Careers activities during imagination week, saw a host of employers and professionals inspire our Key Stage 3 students. The London Fire Brigade's visit was a particular favourite, with a fire engine on site and an engaging insight into careers in the emergency services.
@hafalconwood • 15 July 2026
This June, we proudly celebrated LGBT+ Pride Month 2026, with students and staff taking part in activities that promoted inclusion, allyship, understanding and kindness while celebrating the diversity that makes our community so special.
@hafalconwood • 15 July 2026
We were delighted to showcase the incredible talent of our students at our annual Art & Design Technology Exhibition. The Agora was transformed into a stunning gallery, featuring an impressive collection of GCSE and A Level work for families, staff and students to enjoy.
@hafalconwood • 13 July 2026
Congratulations to all students who took part in our Modern Foreign Languages Spelling Bee! It was fantastic to see such confidence, determination and linguistic talent on display. Well done to everyone involved for representing MFL so brilliantly!
@hafalconwood • 13 July 2026
Year 8 enjoying imagination week with a chocolatey challenge.
@hafalconwood • 13 July 2026
Year 7 had a fantastic day at Leeds Castle! Highlights included seeing baby ducks, meeting a Harris Hawk and other birds of prey, tackling the maze and underground grotto, and exploring the castle while learning about the queens who once lived there. #LeedsCastle
@hafalconwood • 3 June 2026
In RE our Year 9s explored the power of music in religion by creating gospel music pieces. Led by our trainee teacher, Ms Khannom. This engaging and vibrant lesson helped students understand how music can be a powerful medium for expressing and communicating religious beliefs.
@hafalconwood • 20 May 2026
Year 9 trip to the University of Greenwich for Cisco’s Girls in ICT event. Our students took part in the competition and achieved an amazing 2nd place. We so proud of their hard work and teamwork! #serve #support #success
@hafalconwood • 8 May 2026
Year 10 students visited Clifford Chance to learn about careers in law and different pathways into the profession. They also toured the head office in Canary Wharf and experienced the firm’s impressive facilities for staff. #serve #support #success
@hafalconwood • 8 May 2026
— Harris Academy Falconwood (@HAFalconwood) May 8, 2026
@hafalconwood • 24 April 2026
Ms McNeill welcomed many families this morning to the Academy to celebrate the successes of our Year 7 cohort. We were even treated to a song by Riley and Manveer. Well done to all the award winners today. #serve #support #success
@hafalconwood • 24 April 2026
HAF dining hall celebrating St George's Day!
@hafalconwood • 23 April 2026
Mr Christmas invited many Year 8 students to collect their awards today for outstanding performance in their subjects and for upholding our Academy values. We were very pleased to welcome so many families who joined us. #serve #support #success
@hafalconwood • 22 April 2026
Mr Colley was delighted to present certificates to our Year 9 award winners for their dedication to learning and commitment to Academy values. Well done to all our winners. #serve #support #success
@hafalconwood • 21 April 2026
Miss Pello presented awards to our Year 10 subject and PSO winners along with those who were recognised for receiving positive points and for 100% attendance. Well done to all Year 10 winners and thank you to the parents and families for attending. #serve #support #success
@hafalconwood • 21 April 2026
Mr Ali was delighted to present subject and PSO awards to our Year 11 winners. Congratulations to all who received a certificate. #serve #support #success
@hafalconwood • 26 March 2026
— Harris Academy Falconwood (@HAFalconwood) March 26, 2026
@hafalconwood • 26 March 2026
An amazing trip to Madrid and the medieval city of Toledo with our KS3, KS4 & KS5 students! From culture and history to incredible food, tapas and churros included, plus a highlight visit to the Santiago Bernabéu Stadium for our football fans. Memories made and horizons expanded.
@hafalconwood • 26 February 2026
In February we took 24 students to NYC for an unforgettable adventure! From Times Square, the Empire State Building & MoMA to Central Park, the 9/11 Memorial and a sunset walk over Brooklyn Bridge, every moment was incredible. Huge memories made, and we can’t wait to go back!
@hafalconwood • 12 February 2026
A huge thank you to students and staff for engaging positively with our Children’s Mental Health Week wellbeing activities! We’re grateful for the support of the NHS Bexley MHST and resources from @Place2Be in helping create such a calm, supportive space. #serve #support #success
